## Copy to `local.properties` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# The MyAnimeList Client ID this build prefills the sign-in screen with. Register an app at
# https://myanimelist.net/apiconfig with App Type `other` to get one; a public client gets no secret,
# and the ID is not a secret either — it travels in the authorization URL, visible in the user's own
# address bar. So this is convenience and not-in-git, not credential storage.
#
# Three ways to set it, highest precedence first:
#
#   1. `-Pmal.clientId=...`, or a `mal.clientId=...` line in `~/.gradle/gradle.properties` — outside
#      the repo entirely.
#   2. the `MAL_CLIENT_ID` environment variable — the simplest route for CI. Note that
#      `ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_mal_clientId` does *not* work: Gradle does no underscore-to-dot
#      conversion, so it sets `mal_clientId`, which nothing reads.
#   3. the line below.
#
# An empty value at any step falls through to the next, so `-Pmal.clientId=` cannot hide the others.
# Set nowhere, it is empty and the app asks for one — never a build failure. A Client ID typed into
# the app is remembered on that device and wins over this default.
mal.clientId=

# Android SDK location. Written by the IDE; keep whatever is already in your `local.properties`.
#sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/Sdk
